  "summary": "Malicious code in httpnex (PyPI)",
  "details": "Clone of a popular library with added malicious code: during import, package looks for a remote payload to inject into local files, and starts a background thread that periodically re-checks for a new payload. During analysis, C2 did not deliver the payload.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-11-httpnex\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - clones-real-package\n\n",
